  "id": "COMPOUND:30682 - PROTEIN:5829",
  "verbalization": "Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside is implicated in the biological activity of CHP-134 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by Licochalcone D, and both of these compounds ultimately target CHP-134. This indicates a potential pathway where Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside may influence CHP-134 through the activation of SNU-387 or Licochalcone D. The presence of multiple targets in this chain suggests that Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside may exert its effects via a complex network of molecular interactions, possibly involving the modulation of signaling pathways or the activation of specific enzymes. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of understanding the broader biological context in which Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside operates.",
